\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Vehicle normalization pipeline. The raw record $\mathbf  {x}$ is serialized and passed to the LLM for attribute extraction (IE). Closed-domain attributes (dashed bypass) are assigned directly. Open-domain attributes are embedded, matched against a knowledge catalog $\mathcal  {K}_j$ via HNSW, and resolved (ER) by comparing serialized vehicle descriptions. Novel entities expand the catalog.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{3}{Vehicle normalization pipeline. The raw record $\mathbf {x}$ is serialized and passed to the LLM for attribute extraction (IE). Closed-domain attributes (dashed bypass) are assigned directly. Open-domain attributes are embedded, matched against a knowledge catalog $\mathcal {K}_j$ via HNSW, and resolved (ER) by comparing serialized vehicle descriptions. Novel entities expand the catalog}{figure.1}{}}
